<title>FRANCE: German skier hurt in Mont Blanc avalanche.</title>
<headline>German skier hurt in Mont Blanc avalanche.</headline>
<dateline>GRENOBLE, France 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A German skier was in a coma in Chamonix hospital after an avalanche on Thursday swept away eight Germans and Swiss climbing the 4,807-metre-high Mont Blanc, Europe's highest mountain, French police said.</p>
<p>Michael Olbrich, 27, from Erlangen, suffered severe hypothermia after being buried in the snow for half an hour.</p>
<p>Rescuers rushed to the scene after the group's Swiss mountain guide radioed for help. The other climbers were quickly dug out unharmed.</p>
</text>
